# Local scratch: one-shot rollout scripts, PR drafts, throwaway probes.
# A one-shot rollout script is correct exactly once, so it does not belong on
# main. Reusable TESTS do: they live in tests/ and guard-tests.yml runs them on
# every push and pull request. Excluding them would leave the guard's
# correctness unreproducible by anyone but its author, which is what this rule
# was originally, wrongly, used for.
scratchpad/

# Stale leftover from the CI-only code-review-graph build.
.code-review-graph/

# Build artifact, anchored to the ROOT only. `tests/guard/extract.sh` writes the
# extracted guard to `tests/guard/guard.sh` (excluded by the .gitignore next to
# it); a copy at the root can only come from running that extraction by hand in
# the wrong directory, which is how one got committed in 9dc7b0f. Nothing reads
# a root copy, so it could only go stale against merge-on-approval.yml and be
# trusted anyway -- the exact failure `all.sh` re-extracts on every run to avoid.
# The leading slash matters: it must not shadow tests/guard/guard.sh, which is a
# real path the suite writes and reads.
/guard.sh

# Regenerated on every run: tests/check-workflows/run.py exec_module()s
# scripts/check-workflows.py, so every pre-push and every `guard` job rewrites
# this. Tracking it means a stale mirror of the source and a dirty tree for
# everyone.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
